Windows: D3D shared images link without Dawn.

The slim profile has no Dawn (use_dawn, skia_use_dawn false), but
d3d_image_backing.cc on Windows has Dawn paths throughout, which Chrome always
links. They need a Dawn device, which never exists here. Rather than a change
through 2,400 lines, the few symbols they would call are NOTREACHED, in a file
of Windows' alone; only Graphite's representation is left out, since it would
pull in the Dawn classes it derives from.

